# Pull Requests

Only open a PR when the user explicitly asks. Use `gh` for GitHub tasks.
Write titles and bodies in English (match existing PRs).

## Before opening

1. Inspect branch state vs base (`git status`, `git diff`, `git log`,
   `git diff main...HEAD` or the repo’s default base).
2. Push with `-u` if the branch is not on the remote yet.
3. Prefer focused PRs; if a change is large, ask about splitting before opening.

## Title

- Imperative, specific, ≤90 chars, no trailing period
- Prefer the same Conventional Commit shape as commits when it fits:
  `feat(forms): add device preview lab (CYN-11)`
- Or a clear outcome title with ticket ids:
  `Clinical form designer and device preview lab (CYN-11/12)`
- Include Linear/issue ids when known (`CYN-N`)

## Body

Pass the body via HEREDOC to `gh pr create`. Required sections:

```markdown
## Summary
- 1–3 bullets: user-visible outcome or why this change exists
- Not a file list

## Test plan
- [ ] Concrete manual or command checks a reviewer can run
- [ ] Prefer `pnpm typecheck` / `pnpm build` when routes, API, or bundling changed
- [ ] Call out designer vs catalog routes, locale/theme, or narrow viewports when UI changed

Linear:
- https://linear.app/ailuracode/issue/CYN-N
```

Omit the Linear block only when no issue exists. Use `Closes #N` /
`Fixes #N` when linking a GitHub issue.

## Examples

**Title:** `feat(forms): add calculated-field empty state (CYN-11)`

```markdown
## Summary
- Keep calculated fields blank until their source answers exist
- Align preview empty state with designer canvas behavior

## Test plan
- [ ] `pnpm typecheck`
- [ ] Open designer preview → confirm IMC stays empty until weight/height are set
- [ ] Re-check after locale switch

Linear:
- https://linear.app/ailuracode/issue/CYN-11
```

## Anti-patterns

```
# ❌ vague title
Update forms
WIP
fix stuff

# ❌ body is a file dump / no test plan
## Summary
- Changed FormDesignerLayout.tsx
- Updated i18n
```
